/-!
# `Work.G2.LayerC` — the `ℤ`-model of Layer 3 of `thm:CY3` (the CY3 datum, and `notIso`)

This is the **producer** of Layer 3 of the CY3 chapter (`Submission/Work/CY3/Link.lean`, structure
`Work.CY3.CY3Data`) and of the `notIso` field of `Work.CY3.CY3Input` (paper `lem-nSBG2`).

## The three named inputs of this layer

* `K`-triviality and Picard rank one of the two centres (paper `lem-nSBG2`: `Z_𝕜`, `Z'_𝕜` are
  `K`-trivial threefolds of Picard rank one), base-change-uniformly in `𝕜`;
* the two cubic self-intersections `c₁(M_𝕜|_Z)³ = 14` and `c₁(M'_𝕜|_{Z'})³ = 42`
  (Ito–Miura–Okawa–Ueda), base-change-uniformly: the paper computes them as
  `c₁(M_𝕜|_Z)³ = c₁(M_ℤ)³·Z_ℤ` and `c₁(M'_𝕜|_{Z'})³ = c₁(M'_ℤ)³·Z'_ℤ`, i.e. the *same* two numbers
  for every field; together with the named input `Work.G2.CubicInput` (the cubic self-intersection
  is an isomorphism invariant) this **proves** `¬ IsoOver 𝕜 Z Z'` by the arithmetic `14 ≠ 42`;
* the `ℙ¹`-bundle bridge of the link (paper `lemma:L-link` (2) with `m = m' = 2` and (L3)) and the
  two transports `ε : 𝔸⁵ ⇢ G/P`, `δ : G/P' ⇢ 𝔸⁵` with vanishing coefficient at the base point of
  the link (which is what moves the link into the challenge's `Cr 𝕜 5 = Bir(𝔸⁵/𝕜)`).

## What is proved

* `Work.G2.CY3DatumZ.notIso` — the two centres of the `𝕜`-link are not isomorphic over `𝕜`:
  `Work.G2.not_isoOver_of_cubic` applied to the two cubic self-intersections `14` and `42`;
* `Work.G2.CY3DatumZ.toCY3Data` — the `𝕜`-datum `Work.CY3.CY3Data 𝕜`, in which the base point is
  the exceptional divisor `y` itself (`ResEquiv.refl`), i.e. `z₀` has function field `κ(Z)(t)`;
* `Work.G2.CY3DatumZ.toCY3Input` — the input of the CY3 chapter, `Work.CY3.CY3Input 𝕜`, from the
  `ℤ`-model and the isomorphism-invariance of the cubic self-intersection;
* `Work.G2.not_gen_of_G2_infiniteField` — the challenge-level statement: for every infinite field
  `𝕜` and `n ≥ 5`, `Crₙ(𝕜)` is not generated by pseudo-regularizable elements, from the `ℤ`-model,
  the cubic input, Totaro's input (`Work.CY3.TotaroInput`) and the stabilisation input
  (`Work.CY3.CY3Stabilisation`).
-/

